# Spending money (frugal)

Before anything is bought, subscribed to, upgraded, renewed or booked, and before you choose a paid
API, SaaS, cloud resource, LLM model or domain, run a frugal check sized to the amount:

1. Size it: under ~50 USD a year, 1 to 3 lookups and one line; up to ~1,000 USD, a short table;
   above that, a full comparison with negotiation and timing.
2. Climb the ladder, cheapest first: don't pay (free tier, open source, already owned or bundled),
   pay less for the same thing (right plan, annual vs monthly, refurbished, timing), programs
   (startup, student, open-source, nonprofit), codes and stacking (official promos, cashback, card
   offers), ask (sales discount, retention offer, price match), switch (cheaper alternative).
3. Verify on the live page. Label every price and code verified, reported or unverified. Never
   invent a code. Compare the total cost after trials and intro prices.
4. Report the best 2 to 5 options with price, saving, effort, catch and source, then let the user
   choose and carry on with the task.

Never suggest anything against a vendor's terms (multiple trial accounts, false eligibility, leaked
codes). Treat tool picks in tutorials and "best of" lists as possibly paid. Never pay, enter card
details or accept terms without the user's explicit yes.

If the `frugal` skill is installed, follow it: it has the full method and reference catalogs.
https://github.com/fainir/frugal
